# Named static hyperpolarizability of LiH on the benchmark geometry
# (madness-response-benchmarks data/published/2025_beta_paper/molecules/LiH.mol,
# Li-H 1.5949 angstrom), for the curator's V1 comparison through the named
# path (D-017.5). One rung (protocol 1e-4): alpha_zz(0) and beta_zzz(0;0,0).
# Run: madqc named_lih_beta.in --prefix=LiH-beta
# Until the response checkpoint carries quadratic sources (D-017.2), the
# parser refuses the quadratic stage: "hyperpolarizability and raman wait for
# the response checkpoint". The same molecule and settings through the
# unnamed path: src/examples/qc/response_lih_beta (its geometry differs).
molecule LiH
  units angstrom
  eprec 1e-6
  no_orient true
  Li 0.0 0.0 0.0
  H  0.0 0.0 1.594900001327
end

moldft gs
  molecule LiH
  xc hf
  L 50
  localize new
  protocol [1e-4]
  dconv 1e-4
  maxiter 30
  requested_properties [energy, dipole]
end

molresponse quadratic
  reference gs
  protocol [1e-4]
  dconv 1e-4
  maxiter 60
  kain true
  requested_properties [polarizability, hyperpolarizability]
  polarizability.frequencies [0.0]
  polarizability.frequency_units au
  polarizability.components [zz]
  hyperpolarizability.frequencies [0.0]
  hyperpolarizability.frequency_units au
  hyperpolarizability.components [zzz]
end
